===Noun===
{{en-noun|bagmen}}

# {{lb|en|US|Australia|NZ|informal}} A person who [[collect]]s, [[transport]]s, or [[distribute]]s [[illicit]] [[money]], especially for the purpose of [[bribery]], [[extortion]], or the making of other [[improper]] [[payment]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=15 Sep 2006|author=James Graff|title=In France, a Vintage Chirac Scandal is Uncorked|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20091103135808/http://www.time.com/time/world/article/0,8599,1535335,00.html|journal=Time
|passage=The accused are only the latest in a string of alleged '''bagmen''', vote-riggers and ward-heelers charged with wrongdoing.}}
# {{lb|en|golf}} A [[caddy]].
# {{lb|en|Britain|dated}} A staff assistant to a senior police officer (such as a Detective Sergeant for a Detective Inspector).
# {{lb|en|Britain}} A secretary of (and keeper of equipment for) a Morris dancing side<ref>[https://themorrisring.org/publications/morris-tradition The Morris Tradition]'Each club will have... a Bagman who acts as its secretary.'</ref>.
# {{lb|en|Australian|slang}} A [[bookmaker]].
# {{lb|en|Australian|dated|slang}} A [[tramp]], [[hobo]].
#: {{syn|en|vagrant|tramp|bum|hobo|swagman<q:Australia; dated>}}
# {{lb|en|UK|dated|slang}} A [[travel]]ling [[salesman]]<ref>'''1873''', John Camden Hotten, ''The Slang Dictionary''</ref>.
# {{lb|en|US|politics|slang}} An [[officer]] assigned to travel with the [[president]] and carry the "[[football|nuclear football]]".
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1968|journal=Newsweek|volume=72|issue=10-18|page=28
|passage={{...}} in a locked metal suitcase carried on the President's travels by a warrant officer irreverently known as "the '''bagman'''."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Richard Doyle|title=Executive Action
|passage=The '''bagman''' clutching the nuclear football like an undertaker at a wedding. Cameras flashed and clicked, recording the scene. 'Good morning, Mr President,' they chorused.}}
# {{lb|en|Canada|politics|informal}} A prominent [[fundraising|fundraiser]] for a political party or similar cause
#* '''2016''', David Akin, "[https://torontosun.com/2016/05/28/tory-bagman-boasts-about-partys-bank-account Tory 'bagman' boasts about party's bank account], ''Toronto Sun'', 28 May,
#*: Proud to call himself the '''"bagman"''' of the Conservative Party, former senator Irving Gerstein boasted about the financial health of his party Friday.

